From 8b14d18923d1d2074fb4d426c50ebdfd6d808a6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Danylo Piliaiev <dpiliaiev@igalia.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:21:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] vulkan: sort per-binding pNext data in
 vk_create_sorted_bindings

Drivers sort pBindings and then read pBindingFlags and
pMutableDescriptorTypeLists by the sorted position, which is wrong.

The spec indexes these arrays by the position in pBindings, which
doesn't have to be sorted by binding number:

  VkDescriptorSetLayoutBindingFlagsCreateInfo:
    "Otherwise, the descriptor set layout binding at
     VkDescriptorSetLayoutCreateInfo::pBindings[i] uses the flags in
     pBindingFlags[i]."

  VkMutableDescriptorTypeCreateInfoEXT:
    "Otherwise, the descriptor set layout binding at
     VkDescriptorSetLayoutCreateInfo::pBindings[i] uses the descriptor
     type lists in
     VkMutableDescriptorTypeCreateInfoEXT::pMutableDescriptorTypeLists[i]."

Example:

  pBindings = {
     { .binding = 1, .descriptorType = MUTABLE_EXT },
     { .binding = 0, .descriptorType = UNIFORM_BUFFER },
  };
  pMutableDescriptorTypeLists = {
     { STORAGE_BUFFER, SAMPLED_IMAGE },  // pBindings[0], binding 1
     { },                                // pBindings[1], binding 0
  };

After sorting, binding 1 is at position 1, so reading
pMutableDescriptorTypeLists[1] gives it the empty list.

Make vk_create_sorted_bindings take the whole create info and return
a vk_sorted_bindings with the bindings, binding flags and mutable type
lists, all in the sorted order, and all valid to access.

This commit just changes API and doesn't fix anything. The fixes
would be in the follow up commits.

